  OpenCode 1.0 · build mode

› Show me how to read a file in Rust

  Use std::fs::read_to_string:

    use std::fs;

    fn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {
        let text = fs::read_to_string("notes.txt")?;
        println!("{text}");
        Ok(())
    }

  It returns an error when the file is missing.






